-## Subtopics
-
-### Clipping Plane Integration
-Uses clipping planes as a spatial interaction tool to inspect internal volume structures and guide TF design [S1, S2, S4].
-
-### Multi-Dimensional TF Specification
-Particularly useful for multi-dimensional transfer functions (e.g., temperature, humidity, multi-gradient magnitude) where the relationship between features and data values is complex [S6, unofficial].
-
-### Feature-Specific TF Creation
-Allows creation of feature-specific multidimensional transfer functions that would be difficult to produce by manual placement of classification widgets, especially for subtle soft tissues [S5].
-
 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** Real-time interaction. The system must retrieve data values, compute derivatives, update the TF widget, and re-render the volume for every probe movement. This requires efficient data access and rendering pipelines.
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Standard volume rendering memory plus storage for the transfer function (LUT). For 3D TFs, memory consumption increases significantly [S5].
